[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   Step 162 -- NIMA ephemeris-residual pilot on the detached-resident
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   population.
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   The resident channel of the paper rests on discovery-geometry
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   clustering of the detached extreme TNOs.  A logically distinct check
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   is whether the *astrometric residuals* of those same residents carry
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   boundary-organized structure.  The Lucky Star / NIMA programme
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   maintains independent orbit solutions and publishes per-observation
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   O-C files (omc_ast_NIMAvN.txt) for its tracked object list, with the
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   underlying astrometry drawn from MPC plus dedicated WFI/ESO runs --
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   so independence from the comet catalogues is real but partial.
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   This pilot intersects the step_b77 resident ledger with the NIMA
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   object list (parsed from the nima.php page source), downloads the
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   highest-version O-C file per object, parses the fixed-format rows,
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   and builds per-object residual statistics: level, RMS, chi
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   distribution, and a linear drift of O-C versus epoch (an unmodelled
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   ephemeris offset surfaces as a secular slope).  Results are joined
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   to the ledger's axis separation and cap membership.
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   Registered tests
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   T1  coverage ledger: how many detached-resident objects NIMA
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   tracks with usable O-C files, split by cap membership.
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   T2  per-object residual level and drift: |O-C| median/RMS and the
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   fitted O-C-vs-epoch slope with its uncertainty, per object.
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   T3  in-cap vs out-of-cap contrast on residual level and on |drift|
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   -- reported descriptively; with ~7 in-cap objects and ~1
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   control the channel is underpowered by construction and is
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   registered as a pilot, not a detection.
[2026-09-21 15:44:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 162]   Outputs
